I tried to see whether it's possible to compute the selection point without using the DHO reference, and it is and it fixes the crash, but the computation is pretty gnarly...

```csharp
        public override Vector2 ScreenSpaceSelectionPoint
        {
            get
            {
                var column = composer.Playfield.GetColumn(HitObject.Column);
                var hoc = column.HitObjectArea.HitObjectContainer;
                var scrollingPosition = scrollingInfo.Algorithm.PositionAt(HitObject.StartTime, column.Time.Current, scrollingInfo.TimeRange.Value, hoc.DrawHeight);
                var correctedPosition = scrollingInfo.Direction.Value == ScrollingDirection.Up ? scrollingPosition : hoc.DrawHeight - scrollingPosition;
                return hoc.ToScreenSpace(new Vector2(hoc.DrawWidth / 2, correctedPosition));
            }
        }
```

Not sure if too much to be tolerable... It seems like too much. Maybe this can be encapsulated better in `Column` or something, not sure.
